# Accepted image-scan findings (Security.md §5).
# Owner: the release maintainer. Last reviewed 2026-11-03; review again every release.
#
# CVE-2026-34040 (GO-2026-4887): an authorization-plugin bypass in the Moby DAEMON,
# shipped inside the github.com/docker/docker module DockBack imports for its
# client. No github.com/docker/docker release fixes it (the newest is
# v28.5.2+incompatible); the fix is in the daemon module, github.com/moby/moby/v2.
#
# Why it is accepted: the vulnerable code runs in dockerd's AuthZ plugin handling.
# DockBack is only a client and never runs a daemon. govulncheck does list the
# advisory as reachable, but only because the advisory names the whole module
# rather than any function, so every client call matches.
#
# What this does not cover: the daemon on each node is still exposed if it is
# vulnerable and uses an AuthZ plugin. The socket-proxy in front of it does not
# change that. Patch Docker Engine on the nodes.
#
# Remove this entry, and move to a patched client, once one is importable.
CVE-2026-34040
GHSA-x744-4wpc-v9h2
